    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0770" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 P 14/48½a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President and I are very much gratified with your personal and confidential
                    telegram October 26th,<anchor n="35" xml:id="d661-f1"/> and are relieved to hear
                    that the rumors were entire fabrication. Your continued and helpful service is
                    greatly needed in London.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
